# Colour roles and accessibility

Apply GOV.UK’s role-based colour discipline to civica.uk, while preserving our supplied palettes and independent operational meanings. This page explains the decisions behind [Colour](colour.html); it does not introduce another palette. The palette styles the interface; it does not require a civica.uk logo inside a home. The project’s documentation and promotional identity are separate from optional household or business personalisation.

## Choose colours for the task

| Task | Use |
| --- | --- |
| Select interface colours | [Ten palettes and Vivid/Muted](colour.html) |
| Identify a chart series | [Stable categorical chart colours](chart-colour.html) |
| Show increasing values or distance from a target | [Quantitative colour scales](chart-colour.html#choose-the-colour-mapping) |
| Show locations and spatial measurements | [Maps and zones](../home-assistant/maps-and-zones.html) |
| Explain a task visually | [Illustration](illustration.html) |

